cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LLM CAPTCHA Benchmark: interactive CAPTCHA solving and motor-control analysis for multimodal language models"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pavez
    given-names: Diego
repository-code: "https://github.com/kronenflex/llm-captcha-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained benchmark that measures how well local multimodal language
  models solve 28 families of interactive CAPTCHA by driving a real Chromium
  browser through a closed perception-action loop. All fixtures are rendered
  locally and graded server-side by replaying each puzzle's seeded PRNG, so a
  pass never depends on the client's claim. In addition to pass rate, every
  pointer drag is scored on six motor-control metrics derived from the Cerno
  CAPTCHA, giving a measurement of how robotic the agent's motion appears that
  is orthogonal to whether the puzzle was solved. Includes an invisible
  Cloudflare-Turnstile-style family scored on behaviour rather than on an
  answer, a per-family gradient-boosted tool-routing policy learned from
  recorded trajectories, and an optional LoRA fine-tune.
keywords:
  - CAPTCHA
  - benchmark
  - multimodal large language model
  - vision language model
  - browser automation
  - bot detection
  - motor control
  - agent evaluation
references:
  - type: article
    title: "MCA-Bench: a multimodal benchmark for CAPTCHA security"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.05982"
  - type: article
    title: "Open CaptchaWorld"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.07496"
  - type: article
    title: "Set-of-Mark prompting unleashes extraordinary visual grounding in GPT-4V"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.11441"
license: MIT
